A||||2||Roy||What to use for a tranny.
Z||000000||Roy||08-20-99||12:00 AM||||Now that I have started on my 63 Buick v8 conversion. I was wondering what tranny you guys think I should use. Should it be 4 or 5 speed? Price isn't really that much of an issue just no parts that only 100 were made of them:P Let me know what you think I should use. I got everything figured out except for the trans.<p>Roy
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-20-99||07:38 AM||||If price is really no issue, I'd say the 5-sp Getrag is the only way to go.<p>If price is an issue, I'd try the Isuzu.  I've talked to two guys running Isuzus with SB Chevy V8's and neither has had a problem.  V8 Archie also claims the Isuzu can handle up to 300 hp but cautions against "abusive driving."  Isuzus are super cheap to replace, too.<p>If your car will be mainly for show and/or drag runs, the 1984 4-sp might be a good choice. It had a 4.10 final-drive (I can't say rear gear - they're all rear gears!) which would make you launch like a rocket, but you'd be running into redline at about 100-105 mph.
Z||000002||Roy||08-20-99||08:21 PM||||Thanks for the info. I just rebuilt the 4spd that was in it. It has the 4.10 final gear ratio I may use that. But I don't really like having it redlining at 105 or around there.
